# Call-site ledger of whitenoise at 1e3a30bc9e6b82c79a03d35532a7ba72715918df.
# Hand-written from the source; judgements in whitenoise.md.
#
# The scope rules A, B1-B5 and C are in macro-benchmark/README.md;
# whitenoise.md ("Scope rules") shows how this ledger applies them. The
# module-level definitions and their methods are public (rule C). Private
# compression and sorting callbacks receive their package callers' values;
# the regex lambda is public through the immutable_file_test instance
# attribute and retains that predicate role. Public parameters admit opaque
# client objects (B5), package values for their role, and package defaults
# (B2). The WSGI environ and Django's request.META are builtin dicts (B4).
# A directly nested WhiteNoise is a package value in the documented WSGI
# application role. Client-defined applications, server response/file-wrapper
# callables, client header/predicate callables, and Django's get_response
# handler remain opaque (B5). Django names are those of the Django
# 6.0.2 wheel that the test environment pins (read, never run), named through
# the base class that the package names.

